{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0737", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} \\to \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0003": "$i \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0005": "$i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}_i \\to \\colim_i \\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\colim_i H^p(U, \\mathcal{F}_i)\n\\longrightarrow\nH^p(U, \\colim_i \\mathcal{F}_i)\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$p \\geq 0$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$p = 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-section-limits}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-directed-colimits-sections}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:82fde2273c2db7bdebdadc7f0c279e422acdcf13b9de886caaf437417047e19e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ef27f55c4273d59dee7c95a647a1e9fbb742258df696e7766ed6ab8b4fd3904f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>\nbe a diagram over the index category <MATH_0004>, see\nCategories, Section <REF_0001>.\nFor each <MATH_0005> there is a canonical map\n<MATH_0006> which induces\na map on cohomology. Hence we get a canonical map\n<MATH_0007>\nfor every <MATH_0008> and every object <MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010>.\nThese maps are in general not isomorphisms, even for <MATH_0011>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe following lemma is the analogue of\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>\nfor cohomology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c7483a6a5c92800463844405193aa2a6019788825a07061d6b9a8b539191d07c", "unit_id": "tag:0737:prose-0001"}
